WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.742
ALEX: Okay. Claude Ship. Let's
actually explain what this

00:00:02.742 --> 00:00:05.483
ALEX: is, because the name does
not tell you.

00:00:05.593 --> 00:00:07.353
JAMIE: The name sounds like a
logistics startup that

00:00:07.353 --> 00:00:09.112
JAMIE: failed in 2019.

00:00:09.222 --> 00:00:12.325
ALEX: Heh. So — Anthropic released
this on November

00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:15.428
ALEX: twenty-third. It's a suite
of three AI agents

00:00:15.428 --> 00:00:18.531
ALEX: built specifically around
GitHub pull requests. Code Review

00:00:18.531 --> 00:00:21.634
ALEX: is generally available. PR
Steward and Claude Approvals

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:24.737
ALEX: are both in beta.

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:27.535
RUFUS: And the distinction between
those three matters enormously.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.134
ALEX: Tell me.

00:00:28.244 --> 00:00:31.018
RUFUS: Code Review analyses your
code — that's the

00:00:31.018 --> 00:00:33.792
RUFUS: familiar part, AI as
reader. PR Steward goes

00:00:33.792 --> 00:00:36.567
RUFUS: one step further: it
handles merge conflicts, pushes

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:39.341
RUFUS: fixes, responds to
feedback. But it cannot actually

00:00:39.341 --> 00:00:42.115
RUFUS: approve a merge.
